# VibeTune build banner (`vibetune.asm`)

Whenever you produce or refresh **`vtune.com`** (e.g. after meaningful changes, or when the user asks for a build), do **both** of the following **before** running **`Build.cmd`** in this folder:

## 1. Bump the debug build number only (every build)

- Update **`#DEFINE VTBANREL "bNNN"`** only (one token: leading **`b`** + incrementing build number). Examples: **`b144`**, **`b145`**.
- **`VTBANREL` must not carry the software revision.** It is only the rolling debug/build counter.
- **Software revision** stays **`0.1`** until the user explicitly requests a revision change. That revision lives as the literal **`v0.1`** in **`MSGBAN`** (see **`MSGBAN`** `.DB` line: **`"…RomWBW v0.1"`** then **`VTBANREL`**, so the printed form is e.g. **`v0.1b145`**).
- **`VTBANREL`** is also expanded in the **PT3 ident** string (`...Player r.` + token + `=`).

Do **not** add scripts or generated `.inc` files for versioning unless the user explicitly asks for that.

## 2. Banner date = machine “today”, not chat metadata

- **Never** trust Cursor’s injected “Today’s date” / session metadata for the banner string.
- **Do** use the actual calendar date on the user’s machine (e.g. run `Get-Date -Format 'dd-MMM-yyyy'` in PowerShell, or the host OS equivalent) and put that exact string in **`MSGBAN`** after the comma (e.g. `…v0.1b145, 14-May-2026`).

If the shell date is unavailable or ambiguous, ask the user for the date string to embed.

## Workspace note

When the workspace root is the **RomWBW** repo, the same policy is mirrored at **`.cursor/rules/vibetune-build-banner.mdc`** (repo root) with RomWBW-relative paths.
